146500***************************************************************
146600**   CALL 'CBLOWSRT' INSTEAD OF 'TBLOWUP' WHEN A BLOWUP      **
146700**   SITUATION OCCURS SINCE THIS PROGRAM USES THE 'SORT'     **
146800**   VERB.  'CBLOWSRT' WRITES ALL THE BLOWUP INFORMATION     **
146900**   TO A TEMPORARY FILE 'BLUPDATA' (WHICH WAS OPENED AT     **
147000**   THE BEGINNING OF THE PROGRAM) THE CLOSES IT. THEN IT    **
147100**   CREATESA A SON PROCESS 'XBLOWSRT' THAT READS THE        **
147200**   BLOWUP INFORMATION OUT OF 'BLUPDATA' AND CALLS          **
147300**   'TBLOWUP' USING THIS INFO.  SINCE THE NEW PROCESS       **
147400**   'XBLOWSRT' HAS ITS OWN STACK THE STACK OVERFLOW         **
147500**   PROBLEM IS AVOIDED.                                     **
147600***************************************************************
147700
147800     MOVE "TLIFORP2"              TO  BU-PGM-NAME.
147900     CALL "CBLOWSRT" USING CBLOWSRT-PARMS,
148000                           ACCTG-BASE,
